page('1. System overview and how to read the repository')
para('Start with the browser. It loads same-origin static assets from frontend. Every data action uses a relative /api path, routed by the HTTPS ingress to api-gateway. The gateway verifies a session and selects its upstream from a ConfigMap. Each Kubernetes Service selects the current ready Pods; DNS and EndpointSlices track changing Pod addresses. Application code does not contain a fallback Kubernetes hostname or demo database password.')
doc.add_picture(str(out/'architecture.png'),width=Inches(6.8))
table(['Location','Purpose'],[['app/*/src','Service implementations; Node services share app/shared'],['app/shared','HTTP security, config validation, DB pool, tracing, password hashing, migrations, rate limiting'],['app/frontend/src/public','Responsive interface, assets and browser behavior'],['gitops/charts/streamflix','Authoritative v2 consolidated chart'],['gitops/environments','Learning/production configuration and promoted image digests'],['gitops/platform','CA/trust and versioned log-stack configuration'],['.github/workflows','Active CI/publication and deployment jobs'],['scripts/v2','Bootstrap, deploy, validation, promotion, smoke, integration and documentation tooling'],['tests','Node security, Python service and Playwright desktop/mobile tests']])
page('2. User journeys and connection flows')
for name,text in [
('Browse and search','Browser GET /api/catalog/titles → ingress → gateway → catalog-service → catalogdb. Search GET /api/search/search?q=... → gateway → search-service → authenticated Elasticsearch index. Search periodically reconciles from the catalog rather than maintaining a second independently seeded title list.'),
('Register and sign in','Browser POST /api/auth/register → gateway → auth-service. Input is bounded, email normalized and passwords hashed using scrypt with per-password random salt. Login verifies the hash and returns an HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict session cookie. RS256 JWTs enforce algorithm, issuer, audience, subject and expiry. Authentication failures use a generic response; passwords are never returned.'),
('Save a title','Browser PUT /api/users/my-list/:id with its session cookie → gateway verifies JWT → user-service verifies JWT again and uses the subject email for its SQL row. The request does not choose another user’s identity. Watchlist state lives in userdb, so replicas do not share a writable local disk.'),
('Play and resume','Licensed media URLs are catalog metadata. The player accepts HTTPS files from the approved sample host, plays the whole film including credits and periodically stores progress in user-service. Gateway traffic records the view through catalog-service; browser playback remains available if the view-tracking request temporarily fails.'),
('Track viewing asynchronously','Catalog waits for Kafka producer acknowledgement before reporting eventPublished=true. A unique event ID accompanies each event. Activity-tracker consumes the topic and uses one Redis Lua operation to deduplicate the ID and increment a title count. The deduplication window is seven days; this is not a claim of permanent exactly-once processing.'),
('Subscription demonstration','Browser selects a named plan and sends an idempotency key. Billing calculates a fixed amount server-side, persists the response in a transaction, and returns the same response for a repeated user/key pair. It is a sandbox subscription model; no payment provider call or real charge occurs.'),
('Administration','/api/admin/pods requires a valid JWT plus an explicit admin email allowlist. The service uses an in-cluster ServiceAccount and a namespace-scoped Role granting Pod get/list only. There is no public ingress route bypassing the gateway to the old /pods endpoint.')]:
 heading(name,2);para(text)
page('3. Kubernetes components and why they are used')
table(['Component','Role in this project','Operational detail'],[
('Namespace','Scopes application resources in the fresh learning cluster','Learning namespace labels enable restricted Pod Security and public CA distribution.'),('Deployment / ReplicaSet / Pod','Runs stateless HTTP services','Deployment owns rollout history; ReplicaSets own replacement Pods. State moves into datastores.'),('Service / DNS / EndpointSlice','Stable service discovery','ClusterIP/headless Services select ready endpoints; ConfigMap URLs derive namespace and cluster domain.'),('Ingress','Same-origin browser routing and TLS termination','/ goes to frontend, /api goes to gateway; TLS certificate lives in a Secret.'),('ConfigMap','Non-secret environment configuration','Service URLs, DB names, ports, public origin and trace endpoint; checksum triggers application rollout.'),('Secret / ExternalSecret','Credential injection','Secrets are referenced by key. External Secrets fetches provider values; workloads cannot list Secrets.'),('Issuer / ClusterIssuer / Certificate / Bundle','Certificate issuance and CA trust','Learning CA private key stays in cert-manager; trust-manager distributes the public CA only.'),('ServiceAccount / Role / RoleBinding','Workload identity and least privilege','Most workloads disable token mounting. Admin has Pod reads only; platform identities are separate.'),('StatefulSet / PVC / PV / StorageClass','Learning datastore identity and persistence','Four single-node StatefulSets own storage claims. Production uses external resilient datastores.'),('HPA','Scales eligible application Deployments','CPU percentage is relative to requests. Requires metrics-server; scale-down stabilization is five minutes.'),('VPA','Learning resource recommendations','Update mode Off avoids competing CPU adjustments with HPA; requires VPA CRDs.'),('PodDisruptionBudget','Controls voluntary disruption','Multi-replica apps permit one unavailable Pod; single replicas block voluntary eviction.'),('Startup / readiness / liveness probes','Controls startup and routing','Readiness checks dependencies/schema, liveness checks the process; startup avoids premature restarts.'),('Job','Database schema migrations','Versioned SQL and advisory locks; bounded retries/deadline; deployment waits for completion.'),('CronJob','Digest, encoding exercise and DB backup','Forbid overlapping runs, bounded history/deadlines; backup learning PVC retains seven days.'),('NetworkPolicy','Restricts service/data communication','Default deny plus DNS, ingress, metrics and explicit edges. Enforcement requires a compatible CNI.'),('ResourceQuota / LimitRange','Bounds resource consumption','Namespace CPU/memory/Pod/PVC limits plus defaults for containers.'),('SecurityContext / Pod Security','Limits container privileges','Non-root, RuntimeDefault seccomp, all capabilities dropped, no privilege escalation; apps have read-only roots.'),('TopologySpreadConstraint / toleration','Placement and scheduling','Application Pods spread across hostnames; learning datastore Pods tolerate the datastore taint.'),('ServiceMonitor / PrometheusRule','Scraping and alerts','Metrics endpoint discovery, error-rate/restart/unavailable alerts; requires operator CRDs.'),('PeerAuthentication / DestinationRule','Production service mesh','Strict mTLS and bounded connections require running Istio proxies, CNI and an ingress mesh integration.')])
services=[
('frontend','Node / Express','/', 'No private data store','Public static application; three licensed movies and original concept artwork. Browser API calls are relative paths, not configurable user inputs.','No credential Secret is injected. Security headers and CSP restrict script/style/image sources to the application. Movies use an explicit HTTPS host allowlist.','Readiness reports the static server is available. Browser tests cover rendered catalog, dialogs, registration/sign-in UI, search, watchlist and sandbox plans on desktop and mobile.','Static originals and licensed poster assets are shipped in its image. /lab and the legacy public operational console are not exposed.'),
('api-gateway','Node / native Fetch','/api/{service}/*','Redis for shared rate counters','Selects a validated environment-configured origin for each upstream. Removes user-controlled identity headers by forwarding a minimal header set. Preserves session Set-Cookie and idempotency headers. JSON bodies are reconstructed after parsing; requests have timeouts.','JWT is verified before private routes. Public catalog/search/activity reads are explicit. Redis-backed limits work across replicas. CSRF validates the exact public browser origin for cookie-authenticated mutations.','Readiness checks its rate-limit Redis connection. Standard HTTP counters/histograms, request IDs and automatic tracing cover upstream requests.','The gateway is application-level routing. It does not replace Kubernetes Ingress, Service DNS or NetworkPolicies.'),
('auth-service','Node / Postgres / scrypt / JWT','POST /register, POST /login, GET /me, POST /logout','authdb using auth_app','Owns identity records and password hashes. Login performs equivalent password-hash work for unknown accounts, signs a one-hour JWT and sets a Secure HttpOnly SameSite cookie. No JWT is returned for browser storage.','Receives DB credentials, JWT private signing key (auth only), public verification key and Redis password through Secrets. Input bounds and shared rate limiting protect expensive hashing. SQL uses parameters. Generic registration response avoids disclosing duplicate email existence.','Readiness requires users table and Redis. Startup schema work is performed by a migration Job; no app startup DDL.','Logout clears the browser cookie. It does not revoke every already-issued JWT. Short expiry limits exposure; a production account platform should add revocation, recovery, verification, MFA and audited signing-key rotation.'),
('catalog-service','Node / Postgres / KafkaJS','GET /titles, GET /titles/:id, POST /titles/:id/view','catalogdb using catalog_app; Kafka topic','Authoritative title metadata includes posters, duration, rating, genre, licensed playback URL and descriptions. Kafka events have unique IDs and acknowledgements; reads are separate from event publication.','Reads are public catalog data; recording a view requires a JWT. IDs are validated and SQL is parameterized. Database SSL verifies the trusted CA and host.','Readiness requires title schema and connected event producer. HTTP metrics/traces expose latency, failures and DB calls.','Producer retries and idempotence improve reliability, but there is no transactional DB outbox. A browser/client retry may represent a new view event; add request-id deduplication/outbox if durable business events are required.'),
('user-service','Node / Postgres','GET/PUT /profile, GET/PUT/DELETE /my-list, GET/PUT /progress','userdb using user_app','Profiles, watchlist entries and per-title progress are persisted in SQL. Every lookup and mutation derives the user email from a verified session; email is not accepted as a target identity.','Receives its own DB credentials and JWT public verification key. Titles and progress are bounded. Replaces the old path-derived note filename and shared ReadWriteOnce avatar volume to support horizontal replicas safely.','Readiness checks profiles schema; standard HTTP metrics and Postgres tracing apply.','This is one profile per account. Household profiles, uploads/object storage and cross-service catalog referential checks remain extension work.'),
('search-service','Node / Elasticsearch client','GET /search?q=...','Elasticsearch index; catalog API','Periodically reconciles catalog documents into Elasticsearch with stable title IDs. Search matches name, genre and description, returns bounded results and validates query length.','Credentials are Secret-backed. Production uses a least-privilege indexing/search account and HTTPS. Learning uses the bootstrap elastic account in an isolated single-node environment.','Readiness checks Elasticsearch connectivity. Periodic failure logging does not invent results or leak endpoint credentials.','Index freshness is eventually consistent with a one-minute reconciliation interval. Deletes are not reconciled yet; use an event-driven indexing pipeline or full reconciliation when catalog administration is added.'),
('recommendation-service','Python / Flask / Gunicorn','GET /recommendations/:user','Redis cache; catalog API','Retrieves full catalog objects, produces a deterministic user-seeded ordering and caches structured JSON for two minutes. It never falls back to invented title names on dependency failure.','Redis authentication comes from a Secret; URLs are required environment configuration. Recommendations contain public title data only. Private identity/state remains in user-service.','Readiness checks Redis; errors return 503. Flask/Requests/Redis OpenTelemetry tracing and HTTP metrics are wired; Gunicorn runs non-root workers.','This is deterministic content discovery, not a trained recommendation model. Behavioral ranking and privacy-aware feature pipelines can be added later.'),
('notification-service','Node / Redis','POST /notify, GET /notify','Redis per-subject queue','Each authenticated user owns a bounded list of 50 in-app notifications, with a 30-day expiry. The digest CronJob scans queue names without logging user messages.','JWT and Redis password are injected by Secret reference. Message input is bounded. Redis keys use the token subject; another user cannot select the target account.','Readiness returns 503 if Redis is unavailable; metrics and Redis spans are collected.','No email/SMS/push provider is configured. Durable delivery needs provider integration, retry/dead-letter handling and user preferences.'),
('billing-service','Node / Postgres','GET /subscription, POST /subscribe','billingdb using billing_app','Calculates plan prices server-side and uses a user-scoped idempotency key plus a SQL transaction. Replays return the original stored response. Subscriber identity comes from JWT.','Receives DB/JWT/payment Secret references. The provider key is required and never logged, but no provider call is performed. No card input is collected.','Readiness checks subscription schema; failure handling rolls back transactions and returns sanitized errors.','All responses clearly identify sandbox mode. Production billing requires a provider checkout/webhook signature flow, entitlement state, reconciliation, refunds and applicable compliance review.'),
('activity-tracker','Node / KafkaJS / Redis','GET /views/:title','Kafka consumer group; Redis counters','Consumes view events and atomically deduplicates event IDs while incrementing counters with Lua. Deduplication survives replay/consumer restarts within the seven-day retention window.','Redis authentication is Secret-backed. Production Kafka supports TLS/SASL credentials and topic ACLs. It does not expose an event mutation API.','Readiness tracks Kafka consumer startup and Redis state. A dedicated accepted-event counter supports throughput monitoring.','Consumer groups allow scaling, but the learning profile starts one replica. Invalid poison events stop processing until addressed; dead-letter handling and durable analytics are future requirements.'),
('admin-dashboard','Node / Kubernetes client','GET /pods through /api/admin/pods','Kubernetes API, current namespace only','Loads in-cluster credentials and lists a bounded view of Pod name/phase/node. Uses the current client API shape and a namespace supplied through the downward API.','Requires JWT plus configured admin email allowlist. Its ServiceAccount Role permits Pod get/list, with no Secret access or resource mutations. API egress must be allowed explicitly.','Readiness reports process availability. Requests have sanitized errors and standard metrics.','Leave adminEmails empty to deny all administrative users. Administrative authorization should move to a role/claim or identity-provider policy for a real organization.'),
('video-encoder-job','Node batch process','CronJob; no public HTTP endpoint','No external provider in this iteration','Runs the existing seven-step simulated encode exercise as a scheduled non-root container with bounded resources and deadline. Demonstrates CronJob/Job behavior and completion status.','No database, payment or signing secrets are injected into the encoder.','Job success/failure is observed through Kubernetes job state and logs.','It is a simulation, not an FFmpeg transcoder. Production media work requires upload storage, a durable job queue, FFmpeg workers, HLS/DASH packaging, thumbnails and CDN delivery.')]
